From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude Fable 5.1" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 8 Sep 2026 00:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: sdhci-cadence: cdns,single-block-only workaround

On the Axera AX630C the eMMC completes CMD17 and never starts the data
phase of CMD18. The card answers R1 from TRAN, all eight DAT lines stay
high, PRESENT_STATE never shows a transfer active, and a CMD13 after the
failure puts the card back in TRAN -- it does not begin at all, so this
is not a sampling problem. It reproduces on every data path the driver
has (ADMA2 32-bit, ADMA2 96-bit, SDMA, PIO), in HS, HS200 and HS400ES,
in Host Version 3 and 4 mode, open-ended and with Auto CMD12 and with
Auto CMD23, at any address, and BLOCK_GAP_CONTROL is zero throughout.

The cause is not yet known. This is the workaround that makes the board
usable meanwhile: a device tree property that caps every transfer at one
block, so the core splits reads and writes into CMD17/CMD24 loops. It is
deliberately opt-in per board rather than a compatible-wide quirk, and
deliberately ugly, so that it is easy to find and delete once the real
bug is understood.

Signed-off-by: open-nanokvm-pro contributors <nanokvm@localhost>
---
 drivers/mmc/sdhci-cadence.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/sdhci-cadence.c b/drivers/mmc/sdhci-cadence.c
--- a/drivers/mmc/sdhci-cadence.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/sdhci-cadence.c
@@ -292,2 +292,10 @@
+	/*
+	 * Multi-block transfers do not start on this controller. Cap every
+	 * request at one block so the core issues CMD17/CMD24 loops instead.
+	 * See the commit message; delete this with the property.
+	 */
+	if (dev_read_bool(dev, "cdns,single-block-only"))
+		plat->cfg.b_max = 1;
+
 	upriv->mmc = &plat->mmc;
 	host->mmc->priv = host;
